					Title: <b>Lenny Wilkins resigned today</b><br />
					Post by: <b>daps</b> on <b>July 09, 2007, 11:34:27 am</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"> Wilkens leaves NBA Sonics after reorganization<br /><br />Sat Jul 7, 11:16 AM ET<br /><br />Lenny Wilkens, the all-time leader in National Basketball Association coaching victories, resigned as Seattle Supersonics vice chairman here Friday.<br /><br />Wilkens was named the club&#039;s vice chairman last November and promoted to vice president of basketball operations in April when general manager Rick Sund was reassigned and coach Bob Hill was fired.<br /><br />After Wilkens led the search to fill both vacancies, the Sonics hired Sam Presti, 30, to be the general manager last month and gave him all authority on basketball-related issues, kicking Wilkens back to vice chairman.<br /><br />&quot;After much contemplation, I have decided to resign from my position,&quot; Wilkens said. &quot;I feel that my position within the organization did not develop the way that I thought it would.&quot;<br /><br />Wilkens, who has a career coaching record of 1,332-1,155 in 32 NBA seasons, spent 11 seasons as a player or coach of the Sonics, guiding the club to its only league crown in 1979.<br /><br />&quot;Lenny Wilkens has been a valued advisor to me,&quot; said Sonics chairman Clay Bennett said. &quot;His insight into basketball and the Sonics legacy in Seattle helped us greatly as we retooled our basketball operation.&quot;</div>
